matched (per-task) to B's average per-step thought token count (pilot-estimated; e.g., a neutral sentence repeated to match the median per-step thought length). Purpose: separates the reasoning CONTENT from the extra-tokens/time/format overhead confound classic in CoT studies \u2014 any A\u2192B delta attributable to overhead is reproduced in C; B\u2212C isolates reasoning. Runs on the full paired set if budget allows, else a random paired subset (which subset is committed in the manifest).\n\n3) ENVIRONMENT / AGENT-AGENT INTERFACE\n- Harness: BrowserGym browser env hosting ServiceNow-based WorkArena/WorkArena++ tasks. Loop per step: env returns observation \u2192 agent emits response (action [+ thought in B/C]) \u2192 env executes \u2192 reward/step.\n- Observation: flattened/pruned accessibility tree (obs['axtree']) with per-node indices + URL. Identical serialization in all arms.\n- Action space (markdown): click(id), fill(id, val), select_option(id, val), hover, scroll, upload, submit_form, stop. Identical grammar and parser in all arms. Episode ends at task-complete (\"stop\"/goal flag) or at the step cap.\n- The three arms differ ONLY in the inserted instruction/preamble text; harness code, parser, observation, and budget are byte-identical.\n\n4) TASK SELECTION & DIFFICULTY STRATA\n- Task menu: full WorkArena++ suite (WorkArena tasks + WorkArena++ composite/long-horizon tasks). Concrete task/episode counts verified against the repo before execution.\n- Stratum 1 (primary difficulty axis): composition length \u2014 S_single (single-primitive, WorkArena-type) vs S_composite (multi-primitive WorkArena++ long-horizon; the regime where WorkArena++ exceeds WorkArena difficulty).\n- Stratum 2 (domain): workflow taxonomy from the paper (e.g., Knowledge Management, Service Catalog, Candidate Selection, Onboarding, Change Management, Reporting \u2014 verify).\n- Secondary stratum: baseline-difficulty tercile by Arm A success (floor/ceiling detection).\n- All results reported per stratum AND overall; stratum sizes stated so CIs reflect N.\n\n5) EPISODES, SEEDS, PAIRING (trials)\n- Fixed ordered seed set S per task instance (e.g., ~10 seeds/task per WorkArena convention; verify) shared across arms \u2192 PAIRED design: each (task, seed) is one episode run in all arms against identical seeded backend/UI initial state.\n- Arm/order interleaving (randomized across episodes) to average out temporal API drift; run manifest logs model version, date, decode settings, seeds.\n- Greedy decoding (t=0) \u2014 no sampling replicates needed; if any replicate scheme were used it would be R replicates per seed averaged, not part of the primary analysis.\n\n6) METRICS\n- PRIMARY: task success rate \u2014 fraction of (task,seed) episodes reaching task-complete within the step cap, overall and per stratum, with Wilson 95% CI per arm.\n- SECONDARY (1) rubric/primitive partial-success score in [0,1] (WorkArena++ milestone/rubric reward), overall and per stratum \u2014 more sensitive where binary success is rare (S_composite).\n- SECONDARY (2) step efficiency: steps per successful episode and steps-to-complete distributions. Step-cap handling made explicit: the cap (e.g., 30 actions/episode; verify) is applied identically in all arms; budget-exhausted episodes count as failures for the binary metric, while rubric credit still counts already-achieved milestones \u2014 so \"ran out of budget\" is separated from \"executed wrong actions.\"\n- SECONDARY (3) reasoning descriptors (arms B/C): tokens per thought, thoughts per episode, total reasoning tokens per episode; plus a light reasoning-quality proxy \u2014 fraction of steps whose `thought` goal/target element matches the gold primitive (available from WorkArena++ primitive/milestone supervision), scored by deterministic match or LLM-judge on a 10\u201320% stratified sample. Report association (point-biserial/rank) of reasoning length/quality with success, and the per-step token/latency overhead of B/C vs A (feasibility/cost evidence).\n\n7) PRE-SPECIFIED ANALYSIS PLAN\n- Pairing unit: (task, seed) episode; primary comparison A vs B (C is secondary attribution).\n- Primary test: McNemar on discordant binary pairs (overall and per stratum; two-sided \u03b1=0.05). Report p-value, discordant counts b (A-fail/B-success), c (A-success/B-fail), and the paired success-rate difference with a Wilson/ exact-binomial CI on the paired change. Directional interpretation per stratum.\n- Secondary tests: paired Wilcoxon signed-rank on rubric [0,1] scores; bootstrap CIs on the per-stratum mean difference; step-efficiency comparison via paired t/Wilcoxon on steps-per-successful-episode.\n- Sample size & MDES (illustrative, pending verified counts): with n \u2248 N_tasks \u00d7 10 paired episodes per arm (e.g., ~600 pairs) and observed discordance proportion d = (b+c)/n, the detectable paired success-rate shift \u03b4 \u2248 z_{\u03b1/2}\u00b7sqrt(d/n). For d \u2248 0.3 this yields \u03b4 \u2248 1.96\u00b7sqrt(0.3/600) \u2248 4.4 percentage points at 80% power \u2014 i.e., the design is sized to catch a roughly \u00b14\u20135 pt paired shift, which is the scale that would be decision-relevant given the reported low baselines. Exact d and N are re-derived from the verified task menu before execution, and the MDES is recomputed and pre-registered.\n- Multiple comparisons: per-stratum tests are exploratory; correct for the number of strata in interpretation (e.g., report unadjusted plus a simple Bonferroni/Holm note).\n\n8) CONTROLS & FEASIBILITY\n- Controls: identical scaffold, decode, max_tokens, parser, seeds, cap, model version across arms; zero-shot only; arm interleaving; paired same-seed episodes; C isolates token/time/format; primitive-supervised quality proxy anchors \"reasoning\" to something measurable.\n- Feasibility: executing requires cloning the WorkArena++ repo, standing up the ServiceNow backend, and API access for the pinned backbone (network/GPU disabled in this wor